        "original_id": "d98c6362-6b79-554e-b3ca-c27d4d64b943",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Kazan School, Prague School\n- People: Jan Baudouin de Courtenay, Nikolai Trubetzkoy\n- Places: Kazan, Moscow, Vienna\n- Topics: linguistics, structural linguistics\n\nFacts:\n- Kazan School was an influential group of linguists in Kazan.\n- Prince Nikolai Sergeyevich Trubetzkoy was born in Moscow on April 16, 1890.\n- Jan Baudouin de Courtenay was a Polish linguist in the Kazan linguistic circle.\n- Nikolai Trubetzkoy was a student of Jan Baudouin de Courtenay in the Kazan linguistic circle.\n- Nikolai Trubetzkoy was a Russian linguist and historian.\n- Nikolai Trubetzkoy's teachings formed a nucleus of the Prague School of structural linguistics.\n- Nikolai Trubetzkoy died in Vienna on June 25, 1938.",
